{"Race condition between CountDevices and insert/update in CreateOrUpdateDevice - concurrent requests can cause count to be observed as less than deviceLimit but multiple inserts exceed the limit": 0.8519088625907898, "TagDevice is now called synchronously instead of in a goroutine, and errors propagate to Authenticate - this is a breaking behavioral change that could block anonymous authentication when device limit is reached": 0.8050456643104553, "updateDevice returns ErrDeviceLimitReached when rowsAffected == 0, but this could mean device not found or updated_at out of time window - semantics are conflated and should use dedicated sentinel errors": 0.5304303169250488, "Time window logic in updateDevice relies on device.UpdatedAt being now - if UpdatedAt differs or is not normalized, the bounds could be wrong. Should compute now := time.Now().UTC() explicitly in CreateOrUpdateDevice": 0.3758729100227356, "ProvideAnonDBStore and ProvideAnonymousDeviceService signature changes may affect other packages outside this PR - need to verify all call sites are updated": 0.46846482157707214, "When ErrDeviceLimitReached occurs, the code returns it to caller without logging - should log device-limit events explicitly so operators can tell why anonymous auth is failing": 0.7605473399162292, "Missing documentation for auth.anonymous.device_limit INI setting and the behavioral change that tagging is now synchronous": 0.11650412529706955, "anonymouseDeviceExpiration constant is defined in anonstore/database.go and api.go defines anonymousDeviceExpiration - consider centralizing to avoid divergence": 0.21906191110610962, "Missing unit tests for updateDevice to prove return behavior for row-affect zero vs success": 0.506192147731781}